  "notes": "Payload shroud: CONE (corrected from tangent ogive per user 2026-07-28 -- the real AUR fairing is conical), 2.67 m long, body-diameter base (0.8763 m); cone lateral surface pi*R*slant = 3.72 m^2. Mass 22.5 kg from the Akin ENAE 791 fairing MER M=4.95*A^1.15 (same relation as before, re-evaluated for the cone area; was 31.4 kg on the ogive's 4.98 m^2). Physics effect of ogive->cone wave drag + lighter fairing: -73 km range, -31 km apogee on the max-loft reference flight (~2%). Jettison on the heating criterion (q_dot<1135 W/m^2, exoatmospheric).\nStage-1 length corrected 10.2 m -> 5.0 m (user-sourced): the 10.2 was the all-up-round length entered in the stage-1 field (5.0 + 2.6 S2 + 2.67 fairing ~= 10.3 m whole round, matching the ~7,441 kg AUR launch mass bookkeeping).\nBoth stages are solid motors (user, 2026-10-01; were entered as liquid). Stage 1: double-anchor grain (regressive), peak thrust 290 kN (user). Stage 2: grain not given, flown at constant thrust.\nLaunch mass now includes the fairing (user, 2026-10-02): 4,963 (stage 1 fuelled) + 2,028 (stage 2 fuelled) + 22.5 (fairing) = 7,013.5 kg. It was 6,991 kg, the two stages alone, while the fairing's 22.5 kg was still subtracted at jettison.",
